{"name":"Isle of Pines","hex":"#3e6655","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Isle of Pines","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["An island of New Caledonia.","Former name of Isla de la Juventud, Cuba."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Isle_of_Pines"}],"entries":[{"title":"Isla de la Juventud","blocks":[{"text":"Isla de la Juventud is the second-largest Cuban island and the seventh-largest island in the West Indies. The island was called the Isle of Pines until 1978. It has an area 2,200 km2 (850 sq mi) and is 47.1 km (29 mi) south of the island of Cuba, across the Gulf of Batabanó. The island lies almost directly south of Havana and Pinar del Río and is a Special Municipality, not part of any province and is therefore administered directly by the central government of Cuba. The island has only one municipality, also named Isla de la Juventud."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Isla_de_la_Juventud.jpg/330px-Isla_de_la_Juventud.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isla_de_la_Juventud","wikidata":"Q115027"},{"title":"Isle of Pines (island)","blocks":[{"text":"The Isle of Pines is an island in the Pacific Ocean, in the archipelago of New Caledonia, an overseas collectivity of France. The island is part of the commune (municipality) of L'Île-des-Pins, in the South Province of New Caledonia. The Isle of Pines is nicknamed l'île la plus proche du paradis."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Isle_of_Pines.jpg/330px-Isle_of_Pines.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isle_of_Pines_(island)","wikidata":"Q292500"},{"title":"Pine","blocks":[{"text":"Pines ) are a genus of conifers in the family Pinaceae. Pinus is the sole genus in the subfamily Pinoideae. The species are trees or shrubs with their leaves in bunches, usually of 2 to 5 needles. The seeds are carried on woody cones, with two seeds to each cone scale."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Pinus_jeffreyi_at_Lassen_Volcanic_National_Park.jpg/330px-Pinus_jeffreyi_at_Lassen_Volcanic_National_Park.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pine","wikidata":"Q12024"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Presidio_Modelo.JPG/500px-Presidio_Modelo.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Presidio_Modelo.JPG/1280px-Presidio_Modelo.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Presidio_Modelo.JPG/500px-Presidio_Modelo.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Presidio Modelo in 2005","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APresidio_Modelo.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Ile-des-pins.PNG/500px-Ile-des-pins.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Ile-des-pins.PNG/500px-Ile-des-pins.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIle-des-pins.PNG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Noum%C3%A9a_Ile_des_Pins_Upi.JPG/500px-Noum%C3%A9a_Ile_des_Pins_Upi.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Noum%C3%A9a_Ile_des_Pins_Upi.JPG/1280px-Noum%C3%A9a_Ile_des_Pins_Upi.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Noum%C3%A9a_Ile_des_P